      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker replays a captured session cookie against client-portal, which does not bind the credential to the session or channel it was issued for, so the replay is accepted as the original caller. The exposure follows from how client-portal receives operator requests and approval decisions from edge-gateway and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Bind each session cookie to the client certificate or device key, shorten its lifetime to minutes and reject any token presented from a different channel than the one it was issued to. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for client-portal and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "client-portal",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Public Internet/client-portal",
                  "kind": "external-entity"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "61d36056dc09b3dc",
            "findingId/v1": "S-1",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L7 \u2014 Agent Ecosystem",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L7"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A compromised peer presents a forged service identity to partner-feed, and partner-feed accepts the claim without verifying the signature chain back to the issuing authority. The weakness sits at layer Agent Ecosystem of the stack, so every workflow that depends on signed carrier manifests inherits the exposure. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Require mutual TLS between edge-gateway and partner-feed and validate the full certificate chain, issuer and audience on every request instead of trusting the caller's own claim. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "partner-feed",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Public Internet/partner-feed",
                  "kind": "external-entity"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "8114dfb10eff25e1",
            "findingId/v1": "S-2",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L7 \u2014 Agent Ecosystem",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L7"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived webhook signature on partner-feed lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. Because partner-feed serves the Public Internet, a single failure here reaches each consumer of signed carrier manifests at once. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared webhook signature with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for partner-feed and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "partner-feed",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Public Internet/partner-feed",
                  "kind": "external-entity"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "8114dfb10eff25e1",
            "findingId/v1": "S-3",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L7 \u2014 Agent Ecosystem",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L7"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived bearer token on edge-gateway lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. edge-gateway runs in the Edge DMZ and exchanges inbound API requests with reviewer-agent over HTTP/2 over mTLS, so anything able to reach reviewer-agent can also reach this weakness. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared bearer token with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to edge-gateway."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "edge-gateway",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/edge-gateway",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "41828eafe016e25d",
            "findingId/v1": "S-4",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L4 \u2014 Deployment Infrastructure",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L4"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived refresh token on auth-broker lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. policy-engine trusts auth-broker to pass credential assertions and session grants along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared refresh token with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against auth-broker, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "auth-broker",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/auth-broker",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "4cfd16d0f0d8d520",
            "findingId/v1": "S-5",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L6 \u2014 Security and Compliance",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L6"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "Session fixation against intake-agent lets an attacker pre-seed an identifier and reuse the session after the victim authenticates. intake-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges free-text shipment requests with embed-service-2 over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach embed-service-2 can also reach this weakness. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Issue a fresh session identifier on every authentication and privilege change, set strict cookie attributes and invalidate any identifier supplied before login. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to intake-agent."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "intake-agent",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Agent Runtime Zone/intake-agent",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "ed48f56c547e16a5",
            "findingId/v1": "S-6",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L3 \u2014 Agent Framework",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L3",
              "maestro-pattern:trust_exploitation"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "Certificate or DNS spoofing between embed-service-2 and intake-agent lets an attacker terminate the connection and present a lookalike endpoint when pinning is absent. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on free-text shipment requests inherits the exposure. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Pin the expected certificate authority for the link between embed-service-2 and intake-agent, validate host names strictly and fail closed when validation cannot complete. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
