        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "An unauthenticated callback or health route on planner-agent accepts requests that downstream code treats as if they had come from trace-collector. trace-collector trusts planner-agent to pass task plans and tool selections along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Remove implicit trust in route names: authenticate every route of planner-agent, including callbacks and health checks, and drop requests that carry no verified caller identity. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against planner-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
