        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "Session fixation against planner-agent lets an attacker pre-seed an identifier and reuse the session after the victim authenticates. Because planner-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of task plans and tool selections at once. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Issue a fresh session identifier on every authentication and privilege change, set strict cookie attributes and invalidate any identifier supplied before login. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
