        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived routing token on router-agent lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on subtask assignments inherits the exposure. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared routing token with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to router-agent."
          },
          "level": "warning",
