        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "An unauthenticated callback or health route on router-agent accepts requests that downstream code treats as if they had come from worker-3. Because router-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of subtask assignments at once. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Remove implicit trust in route names: authenticate every route of router-agent, including callbacks and health checks, and drop requests that carry no verified caller identity. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against router-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
