        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "Certificate or DNS spoofing between trace-collector and worker-3 lets an attacker terminate the connection and present a lookalike endpoint when pinning is absent. worker-3 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges work orders and draft documents with trace-collector over OTLP over TLS, so anything able to reach trace-collector can also reach this weakness. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Pin the expected certificate authority for the link between trace-collector and worker-3, validate host names strictly and fail closed when validation cannot complete. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "warning",
