        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "Low-entropy identifiers accepted by worker-3 double as credentials, so an attacker who enumerates them submits requests under a victim's identity. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on work orders and draft documents inherits the exposure. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Separate identifiers from secrets, generate secrets from a cryptographic random source of at least 128 bits and rate-limit failed lookups against worker-3. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
