        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker replays a captured worker credential against worker-3, which does not bind the credential to the session or channel it was issued for, so the replay is accepted as the original caller. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on work orders and draft documents inherits the exposure. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Bind each worker credential to the client certificate or device key, shorten its lifetime to minutes and reject any token presented from a different channel than the one it was issued to. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to worker-3."
