            "text": "A compromised peer presents a forged service identity to embed-service-2, and embed-service-2 accepts the claim without verifying the signature chain back to the issuing authority. The weakness sits at layer Foundation Model of the stack, so every workflow that depends on document chunks and query embeddings inherits the exposure. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Require mutual TLS between intake-agent and embed-service-2 and validate the full certificate chain, issuer and audience on every request instead of trusting the caller's own claim. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for embed-service-2 and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
