        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived service credential on embed-service-2 lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. embed-service-2 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges document chunks and query embeddings with kb-index over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach kb-index can also reach this weakness. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared service credential with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
