        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "Low-entropy identifiers accepted by summarizer-llm double as credentials, so an attacker who enumerates them submits requests under a victim's identity. summarizer-llm runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges shipment records fed into summaries with worker-3 over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach worker-3 can also reach this weakness. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Separate identifiers from secrets, generate secrets from a cryptographic random source of at least 128 bits and rate-limit failed lookups against summarizer-llm. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against summarizer-llm, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
