        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker replays a captured inference credential against summarizer-llm, which does not bind the credential to the session or channel it was issued for, so the replay is accepted as the original caller. The weakness sits at layer Foundation Model of the stack, so every workflow that depends on shipment records fed into summaries inherits the exposure. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Bind each inference credential to the client certificate or device key, shorten its lifetime to minutes and reject any token presented from a different channel than the one it was issued to. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
