            "text": "An unauthenticated callback or health route on edge-gateway accepts requests that downstream code treats as if they had come from auth-broker. Because edge-gateway serves the Edge DMZ, a single failure here reaches each consumer of inbound API requests at once. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Remove implicit trust in route names: authenticate every route of edge-gateway, including callbacks and health checks, and drop requests that carry no verified caller identity. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against edge-gateway, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
