        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker replays a captured reviewer session against reviewer-agent, which does not bind the credential to the session or channel it was issued for, so the replay is accepted as the original caller. reviewer-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges drafted proposals awaiting review with summarizer-llm over HTTP/2 over mTLS, so anything able to reach summarizer-llm can also reach this weakness. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Bind each reviewer session to the client certificate or device key, shorten its lifetime to minutes and reject any token presented from a different channel than the one it was issued to. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
