        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A compromised peer presents a forged service identity to reviewer-agent, and reviewer-agent accepts the claim without verifying the signature chain back to the issuing authority. summarizer-llm trusts reviewer-agent to pass drafted proposals awaiting review along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Require mutual TLS between summarizer-llm and reviewer-agent and validate the full certificate chain, issuer and audience on every request instead of trusting the caller's own claim. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for reviewer-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
