        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A compromised peer presents a forged service identity to model-gateway, and model-gateway accepts the claim without verifying the signature chain back to the issuing authority. The exposure follows from how model-gateway receives prompts and completions from planner-agent and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Require mutual TLS between planner-agent and model-gateway and validate the full certificate chain, issuer and audience on every request instead of trusting the caller's own claim. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
