        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker who can write to the channel between client-portal and edge-gateway modifies inbound API requests in transit because messages carry no integrity protection of their own. The weakness sits at layer Deployment Infrastructure of the stack, so every workflow that depends on inbound API requests inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Sign messages between client-portal and edge-gateway with a per-service key and verify the signature and a monotonic counter before accepting any change. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
