        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Backups and exports of credential assertions and session grants on auth-broker are writable by operators without a second approver, so a malicious change survives restores. auth-broker runs in the Edge DMZ and exchanges credential assertions and session grants with edge-gateway over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach edge-gateway can also reach this weakness. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Protect exports and backups of credential assertions and session grants with write-once storage and dual approval for restore, and verify checksums against a separately held manifest. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
