        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unsanitised task plans and tool selections reach planner-agent and are processed as trusted structure, so crafted input changes how later steps interpret the record. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on task plans and tool selections inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Validate task plans and tool selections against a strict schema at the boundary of planner-agent, reject unknown fields and normalise encodings before any downstream use. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against planner-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
