          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "A race between concurrent writers lets an attacker overwrite prompts and completions on model-gateway after validation but before use, defeating the earlier check. planner-agent trusts model-gateway to pass prompts and completions along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Make validation and use atomic: take a version-checked write or compare-and-set on prompts and completions, and reject updates whose version no longer matches. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
