        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Replay of an earlier valid update to prompts and completions reaches model-gateway because updates carry no nonce or expiry, restoring a state the owner already corrected. The weakness sits at layer Foundation Model of the stack, so every workflow that depends on prompts and completions inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Add a nonce and a short expiry to every update accepted by model-gateway, store seen nonces for the validity window and reject any repeat. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against model-gateway, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
