        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Replay of an earlier valid update to document chunks and query embeddings reaches embed-service-2 because updates carry no nonce or expiry, restoring a state the owner already corrected. The exposure follows from how embed-service-2 receives document chunks and query embeddings from vector-store-a and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Add a nonce and a short expiry to every update accepted by embed-service-2, store seen nonces for the validity window and reject any repeat. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against embed-service-2, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
