        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Backups and exports of shipment records fed into summaries on summarizer-llm are writable by operators without a second approver, so a malicious change survives restores. Because summarizer-llm serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of shipment records fed into summaries at once. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Protect exports and backups of shipment records fed into summaries with write-once storage and dual approval for restore, and verify checksums against a separately held manifest. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for summarizer-llm and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
