        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Serialised objects arriving from worker-2 are deserialised by vector-store-a with permissive type handling, allowing crafted payloads to instantiate unintended behaviour. The weakness sits at layer Data Operations of the stack, so every workflow that depends on embedded documents and metadata inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Replace permissive deserialisation in vector-store-a with a closed schema of allowed types, and reject payloads that name types outside it. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for vector-store-a and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
