        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Backups and exports of embedded documents and metadata on vector-store-a are writable by operators without a second approver, so a malicious change survives restores. worker-2 trusts vector-store-a to pass embedded documents and metadata along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Protect exports and backups of embedded documents and metadata with write-once storage and dual approval for restore, and verify checksums against a separately held manifest. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to vector-store-a."
