        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unsanitised embedded documents and metadata reach vector-store-a and are processed as trusted structure, so crafted input changes how later steps interpret the record. The exposure follows from how vector-store-a receives embedded documents and metadata from worker-2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Validate embedded documents and metadata against a strict schema at the boundary of vector-store-a, reject unknown fields and normalise encodings before any downstream use. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for vector-store-a and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
