        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unsanitised archived transcripts and training corpora reach s3-archive and are processed as trusted structure, so crafted input changes how later steps interpret the record. The weakness sits at layer Data Operations of the stack, so every workflow that depends on archived transcripts and training corpora inherits the exposure. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Validate archived transcripts and training corpora against a strict schema at the boundary of s3-archive, reject unknown fields and normalise encodings before any downstream use. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for s3-archive and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
