        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "An update to feature-store-2 is pulled without provenance checks, so a poisoned package can alter how ranking and fine-tuning features are handled at run time. The weakness sits at layer Data Operations of the stack, so every workflow that depends on ranking and fine-tuning features inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Pin dependencies by digest, verify signatures and provenance attestations in CI, and block deployment of feature-store-2 when a component lacks a valid attestation. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
