          "message": {
            "text": "A race between concurrent writers lets an attacker overwrite task and result messages on queue-a2 after validation but before use, defeating the earlier check. The exposure follows from how queue-a2 receives task and result messages from scheduler-1 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Make validation and use atomic: take a version-checked write or compare-and-set on task and result messages, and reject updates whose version no longer matches. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
