          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Configuration of scheduler-1 can be rewritten by any service that holds the shared deployment credential, silently changing how recurring planning triggers are handled. scheduler-1 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges recurring planning triggers with queue-a2 over NATS over TLS, so anything able to reach queue-a2 can also reach this weakness. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Keep the configuration of scheduler-1 in a versioned, access-controlled repository, require review for changes and alert on drift from the approved revision. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
