          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Serialised objects arriving from trace-collector are deserialised by eval-runner with permissive type handling, allowing crafted payloads to instantiate unintended behaviour. The weakness sits at layer Evaluation and Observability of the stack, so every workflow that depends on replayed traces and judge verdicts inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Replace permissive deserialisation in eval-runner with a closed schema of allowed types, and reject payloads that name types outside it. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to eval-runner."
