        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Replay of an earlier valid update to guardrail rules and approval decisions reaches policy-engine because updates carry no nonce or expiry, restoring a state the owner already corrected. planner-agent trusts policy-engine to pass guardrail rules and approval decisions along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Add a nonce and a short expiry to every update accepted by policy-engine, store seen nonces for the validity window and reject any repeat. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
