        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Serialised objects arriving from audit-ledger are deserialised by policy-engine with permissive type handling, allowing crafted payloads to instantiate unintended behaviour. Because policy-engine serves the Operations Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of guardrail rules and approval decisions at once. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Replace permissive deserialisation in policy-engine with a closed schema of allowed types, and reject payloads that name types outside it. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
