        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Backups and exports of guardrail rules and approval decisions on policy-engine are writable by operators without a second approver, so a malicious change survives restores. The exposure follows from how policy-engine receives guardrail rules and approval decisions from auth-broker and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Protect exports and backups of guardrail rules and approval decisions with write-once storage and dual approval for restore, and verify checksums against a separately held manifest. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for policy-engine and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
