        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker who can write to the channel between reviewer-agent and audit-ledger modifies approval and tool call records in transit because messages carry no integrity protection of their own. Because audit-ledger serves the Operations Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of approval and tool call records at once. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Sign messages between reviewer-agent and audit-ledger with a per-service key and verify the signature and a monotonic counter before accepting any change. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
