        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker who can write to the channel between trace-collector and worker-2 modifies work orders and route candidates in transit because messages carry no integrity protection of their own. worker-2 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges work orders and route candidates with trace-collector over OTLP over TLS, so anything able to reach trace-collector can also reach this weakness. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Sign messages between trace-collector and worker-2 with a per-service key and verify the signature and a monotonic counter before accepting any change. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against worker-2, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "worker-2",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Agent Runtime Zone/worker-2",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "4543121a8b76a5c2",
            "findingId/v1": "T-44",
            "baselineRunId": ""
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "new",
            "maestro-layer": "L3 \u2014 Agent Framework",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L3"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "An update to worker-3 is pulled without provenance checks, so a poisoned package can alter how work orders and draft documents are handled at run time. worker-3 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges work orders and draft documents with tool-server-1 over HTTPS (TLS 1.3), so anything able to reach tool-server-1 can also reach this weakness. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Pin dependencies by digest, verify signatures and provenance attestations in CI, and block deployment of worker-3 when a component lacks a valid attestation. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against worker-3, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
