        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Configuration of reviewer-agent can be rewritten by any service that holds the shared deployment credential, silently changing how drafted proposals awaiting review are handled. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on drafted proposals awaiting review inherits the exposure. The change can persist across restarts and restores, which makes the original state difficult to prove and to recover. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Keep the configuration of reviewer-agent in a versioned, access-controlled repository, require review for changes and alert on drift from the approved revision. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to reviewer-agent."
          },
          "level": "warning",
