        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Operators approve changes to operator requests and approval decisions through a chat message or ticket comment that is not bound to the executed change, so approvals can be disputed. Because client-portal serves the Public Internet, a single failure here reaches each consumer of operator requests and approval decisions at once. Without reliable records an investigation cannot establish who acted, so disputes about responsibility stay unresolved. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Bind each approval to the exact change hash it covers, record approver and time in the audit ledger and refuse to execute unbound changes. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to client-portal."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
