        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Clock drift between partner-feed and edge-gateway leaves events in inconsistent order, so the sequence of actions on signed carrier manifests cannot be reconstructed reliably. The weakness sits at layer Agent Ecosystem of the stack, so every workflow that depends on signed carrier manifests inherits the exposure. Without reliable records an investigation cannot establish who acted, so disputes about responsibility stay unresolved. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Synchronise partner-feed and edge-gateway to a trusted time source, record monotonic sequence numbers with every event and alert when drift exceeds one second. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for partner-feed and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
