        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Log entries from edge-gateway can be edited or deleted by the same operators who administer it, so evidence of misuse can be removed after the fact. The weakness sits at layer Deployment Infrastructure of the stack, so every workflow that depends on inbound API requests inherits the exposure. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Write the records of edge-gateway to an append-only store that operators cannot modify, and anchor periodic hashes of the log in a separate system. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
