          "message": {
            "text": "Clock drift between edge-gateway and client-portal leaves events in inconsistent order, so the sequence of actions on inbound API requests cannot be reconstructed reliably. The exposure follows from how edge-gateway receives inbound API requests from client-portal and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
