        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Delegated actions performed by auth-broker on behalf of a user are recorded under the service identity alone, hiding who authorised them. auth-broker runs in the Edge DMZ and exchanges credential assertions and session grants with edge-gateway over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach edge-gateway can also reach this weakness. Without reliable records an investigation cannot establish who acted, so disputes about responsibility stay unresolved. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Carry the originating user and the approval reference through every delegated call made by auth-broker, and record both in the audit entry. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
