        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Operators approve changes to task plans and tool selections through a chat message or ticket comment that is not bound to the executed change, so approvals can be disputed. The exposure follows from how planner-agent receives task plans and tool selections from queue-a2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Bind each approval to the exact change hash it covers, record approver and time in the audit ledger and refuse to execute unbound changes. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "warning",
