        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Actions taken through router-agent are logged without the authenticated principal or a request identifier, so a caller can deny having submitted a change to subtask assignments. planner-agent trusts router-agent to pass subtask assignments along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Log the verified principal, request identifier, source address and outcome for every state change in router-agent, and ship the records to the audit ledger. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for router-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
