        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Log entries from router-agent can be edited or deleted by the same operators who administer it, so evidence of misuse can be removed after the fact. The exposure follows from how router-agent receives subtask assignments from worker-2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Without reliable records an investigation cannot establish who acted, so disputes about responsibility stay unresolved. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Write the records of router-agent to an append-only store that operators cannot modify, and anchor periodic hashes of the log in a separate system. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to router-agent."
          },
          "level": "error",
