        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Clock drift between embed-service-2 and vector-store-a leaves events in inconsistent order, so the sequence of actions on document chunks and query embeddings cannot be reconstructed reliably. embed-service-2 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges document chunks and query embeddings with vector-store-a over PostgreSQL over TLS, so anything able to reach vector-store-a can also reach this weakness. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Synchronise embed-service-2 and vector-store-a to a trusted time source, record monotonic sequence numbers with every event and alert when drift exceeds one second. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against embed-service-2, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
