        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Delegated actions performed by embed-service-2 on behalf of a user are recorded under the service identity alone, hiding who authorised them. Because embed-service-2 serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of document chunks and query embeddings at once. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Carry the originating user and the approval reference through every delegated call made by embed-service-2, and record both in the audit entry. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against embed-service-2, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
