          "message": {
            "text": "Actions taken through summarizer-llm are logged without the authenticated principal or a request identifier, so a caller can deny having submitted a change to shipment records fed into summaries. worker-3 trusts summarizer-llm to pass shipment records fed into summaries along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Log the verified principal, request identifier, source address and outcome for every state change in summarizer-llm, and ship the records to the audit ledger. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
