          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Clock drift between scheduler-1 and queue-a2 leaves events in inconsistent order, so the sequence of actions on recurring planning triggers cannot be reconstructed reliably. scheduler-1 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges recurring planning triggers with queue-a2 over NATS over TLS, so anything able to reach queue-a2 can also reach this weakness. Without reliable records an investigation cannot establish who acted, so disputes about responsibility stay unresolved. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Synchronise scheduler-1 and queue-a2 to a trusted time source, record monotonic sequence numbers with every event and alert when drift exceeds one second. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to scheduler-1."
          },
