        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Operators approve changes to prompts, completions and tool traces through a chat message or ticket comment that is not bound to the executed change, so approvals can be disputed. Because trace-collector serves the Operations Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of prompts, completions and tool traces at once. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Bind each approval to the exact change hash it covers, record approver and time in the audit ledger and refuse to execute unbound changes. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against trace-collector, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
