          "message": {
            "text": "Operators approve changes to guardrail rules and approval decisions through a chat message or ticket comment that is not bound to the executed change, so approvals can be disputed. The weakness sits at layer Security and Compliance of the stack, so every workflow that depends on guardrail rules and approval decisions inherits the exposure. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
