        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Secrets such as the bearer token for edge-gateway appear in process arguments and environment dumps that diagnostic tooling captures. Because edge-gateway serves the Edge DMZ, a single failure here reaches each consumer of inbound API requests at once. The exposed material can be reused for follow-on attacks and may trigger notification duties if it covers customer data. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Pass the bearer token to edge-gateway through a secret manager mount, exclude it from process listings and diagnostics, and rotate it after any exposure. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
