        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cross-tenant filters on planner-agent are applied in application code only, so one missing predicate exposes another tenant's task plans and tool selections. Because planner-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of task plans and tool selections at once. The exposed material can be reused for follow-on attacks and may trigger notification duties if it covers customer data. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Enforce tenant isolation in the data layer with row-level policies or separate keys, and add a regression test that queries across tenants. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
