          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "A timing or size difference in the responses of router-agent lets an observer infer whether specific records of subtask assignments exist. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on subtask assignments inherits the exposure. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Equalise response size and timing for existence checks in router-agent, and return the same status for present and absent records. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for router-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
