        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "carrier tariffs and customs rules held by kb-index are readable by any service in the Data Zone that shares the same network role, because access is granted by network position. The weakness sits at layer Data Operations of the stack, so every workflow that depends on carrier tariffs and customs rules inherits the exposure. The exposed material can be reused for follow-on attacks and may trigger notification duties if it covers customer data. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
