              "maestro-layer:L2"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cross-tenant filters on memory-store are applied in application code only, so one missing predicate exposes another tenant's task history and operator preferences. The weakness sits at layer Data Operations of the stack, so every workflow that depends on task history and operator preferences inherits the exposure. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Enforce tenant isolation in the data layer with row-level policies or separate keys, and add a regression test that queries across tenants. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for memory-store and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
