        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Data in transit between trace-collector and s3-archive is protected only on the outer hop, which leaves archived transcripts and training corpora readable on the internal segment after termination. s3-archive runs in the Data Zone and exchanges archived transcripts and training corpora with trace-collector over HTTPS (TLS 1.3), so anything able to reach trace-collector can also reach this weakness. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Keep TLS end to end between trace-collector and s3-archive, disable plaintext listeners and verify the negotiated protocol version in deployment checks. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
