        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "A timing or size difference in the responses of queue-a2 lets an observer infer whether specific records of task and result messages exist. The exposure follows from how queue-a2 receives task and result messages from planner-agent and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The exposed material can be reused for follow-on attacks and may trigger notification duties if it covers customer data. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Equalise response size and timing for existence checks in queue-a2, and return the same status for present and absent records. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
