        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Logs and traces emitted by policy-engine include raw guardrail rules and approval decisions, so anyone with access to the logging pipeline can read content meant for one tenant. policy-engine runs in the Operations Zone and exchanges guardrail rules and approval decisions with audit-ledger over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach audit-ledger can also reach this weakness. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Redact or tokenise sensitive fields before policy-engine emits logs and traces, and restrict the logging pipeline to the roles that need it. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
