          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Logs and traces emitted by audit-ledger include raw approval and tool call records, so anyone with access to the logging pipeline can read content meant for one tenant. The weakness sits at layer Security and Compliance of the stack, so every workflow that depends on approval and tool call records inherits the exposure. The exposed material can be reused for follow-on attacks and may trigger notification duties if it covers customer data. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Redact or tokenise sensitive fields before audit-ledger emits logs and traces, and restrict the logging pipeline to the roles that need it. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
