          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Logs and traces emitted by edge-gateway include raw inbound API requests, so anyone with access to the logging pipeline can read content meant for one tenant. The weakness sits at layer Deployment Infrastructure of the stack, so every workflow that depends on inbound API requests inherits the exposure. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Redact or tokenise sensitive fields before edge-gateway emits logs and traces, and restrict the logging pipeline to the roles that need it. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for edge-gateway and record any exception with an expiry date."
