        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "A timing or size difference in the responses of s3-archive lets an observer infer whether specific records of archived transcripts and training corpora exist. trace-collector trusts s3-archive to pass archived transcripts and training corpora along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Equalise response size and timing for existence checks in s3-archive, and return the same status for present and absent records. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
