        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Data in transit between audit-ledger and policy-engine is protected only on the outer hop, which leaves guardrail rules and approval decisions readable on the internal segment after termination. audit-ledger trusts policy-engine to pass guardrail rules and approval decisions along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Keep TLS end to end between audit-ledger and policy-engine, disable plaintext listeners and verify the negotiated protocol version in deployment checks. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against policy-engine, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
