            "maestro-layer": "L6 \u2014 Security and Compliance",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L6"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/denial-of-service",
          "message": {
            "text": "Retry storms from edge-gateway multiply the load on auth-broker when it slows down, turning a brief delay into a sustained outage. Because auth-broker serves the Edge DMZ, a single failure here reaches each consumer of credential assertions and session grants at once. The outage propagates to dependent agents, which stall or retry and prolong the disruption. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Add jittered exponential backoff and a retry budget to edge-gateway, and enable a circuit breaker so that auth-broker can recover. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against auth-broker, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
