          "message": {
            "text": "A slow-read attack holds connections to tool-server-1 open and ties up the workers handling tool call arguments and results until none remain for real requests. tool-server-1 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges tool call arguments and results with audit-ledger over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach audit-ledger can also reach this weakness. The outage propagates to dependent agents, which stall or retry and prolong the disruption. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Apply idle and total timeouts on every connection to tool-server-1, bound workers per client and move slow clients to a separate pool. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
