          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/denial-of-service",
          "message": {
            "text": "A single oversized or deeply nested payload makes summarizer-llm spend disproportionate memory and CPU parsing shipment records fed into summaries. reviewer-agent trusts summarizer-llm to pass shipment records fed into summaries along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Operators lose the ability to book or amend shipments while the condition lasts, and recovery depends on manual intervention. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Cap payload size, nesting depth and parse time in summarizer-llm, and reject requests that exceed the limits before allocation. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against summarizer-llm, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
