          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/denial-of-service",
          "message": {
            "text": "Retry storms from embed-service-2 multiply the load on vector-store-a when it slows down, turning a brief delay into a sustained outage. Because vector-store-a serves the Data Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of embedded documents and metadata at once. Operators lose the ability to book or amend shipments while the condition lasts, and recovery depends on manual intervention. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Add jittered exponential backoff and a retry budget to embed-service-2, and enable a circuit breaker so that vector-store-a can recover. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for vector-store-a and record any exception with an expiry date."
