        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/denial-of-service",
          "message": {
            "text": "Expensive queries over guardrail rules and approval decisions can be triggered by any authorised caller of policy-engine, so one user can degrade the service for all. The weakness sits at layer Security and Compliance of the stack, so every workflow that depends on guardrail rules and approval decisions inherits the exposure. The outage propagates to dependent agents, which stall or retry and prolong the disruption. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Enforce cost limits and pagination on queries to policy-engine, run heavy work on a separate pool and cancel queries that exceed the budget. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against policy-engine, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
