        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/denial-of-service",
          "message": {
            "text": "A slow-read attack holds connections to worker-2 open and ties up the workers handling work orders and route candidates until none remain for real requests. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on work orders and route candidates inherits the exposure. The outage propagates to dependent agents, which stall or retry and prolong the disruption. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Apply idle and total timeouts on every connection to worker-2, bound workers per client and move slow clients to a separate pool. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to worker-2."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
