        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "Object identifiers in requests to edge-gateway are trusted without an ownership check, so a caller can read or change inbound API requests that belong to others. The weakness sits at layer Deployment Infrastructure of the stack, so every workflow that depends on inbound API requests inherits the exposure. Once the boundary is crossed the attacker can reach administrative functions and persist there. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Check ownership or entitlement for every object reference at edge-gateway on the server, and deny by default when the check cannot be made. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "edge-gateway",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/edge-gateway",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "b519ad7937a2e79a",
            "findingId/v1": "E-1",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L4 \u2014 Deployment Infrastructure",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L4"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "Role claims carried in the bearer token presented to edge-gateway are honoured without confirmation against the authoritative directory. intake-agent trusts edge-gateway to pass inbound API requests along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The caller gains rights that were never granted, which allows reading and changing data across tenants and approvals. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Resolve roles for edge-gateway from the authoritative directory on each request or from a short cache, and ignore role claims supplied by the caller. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "edge-gateway",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/edge-gateway",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "b519ad7937a2e79a",
            "findingId/v1": "E-2",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L4 \u2014 Deployment Infrastructure",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L4"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "An administrative interface of edge-gateway is reachable from the same network as ordinary callers and relies on a single shared password. Because edge-gateway serves the Edge DMZ, a single failure here reaches each consumer of inbound API requests at once. Once the boundary is crossed the attacker can reach administrative functions and persist there. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Move the administrative interface of edge-gateway behind a separate listener with strong authentication, network restriction and per-user accounts. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to edge-gateway."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "edge-gateway",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/edge-gateway",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "b519ad7937a2e79a",
            "findingId/v1": "E-3",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L4 \u2014 Deployment Infrastructure",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L4"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "edge-gateway runs with broader permissions than its function needs, so a flaw in handling inbound API requests yields access to unrelated resources. edge-gateway runs in the Edge DMZ and exchanges inbound API requests with partner-feed over HTTPS (TLS 1.3), so anything able to reach partner-feed can also reach this weakness. Once the boundary is crossed the attacker can reach administrative functions and persist there. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Reduce the permissions of edge-gateway to the minimum for inbound API requests, drop capabilities it does not use and review the grants on a schedule. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against edge-gateway, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
