          "message": {
            "text": "Role claims carried in the refresh token presented to auth-broker are honoured without confirmation against the authoritative directory. Because auth-broker serves the Edge DMZ, a single failure here reaches each consumer of credential assertions and session grants at once. The caller gains rights that were never granted, which allows reading and changing data across tenants and approvals. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Resolve roles for auth-broker from the authoritative directory on each request or from a short cache, and ignore role claims supplied by the caller. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
