        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "Multi-tenant separation in router-agent depends on a request header that clients can set, allowing one tenant to act in another's scope. router-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges subtask assignments with planner-agent over HTTP/2 over mTLS, so anything able to reach planner-agent can also reach this weakness. The caller gains rights that were never granted, which allows reading and changing data across tenants and approvals. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Derive the tenant for router-agent from the verified credential, ignore client-supplied tenant headers and test cross-tenant requests in CI. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for router-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
