        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "Multi-tenant separation in reviewer-agent depends on a request header that clients can set, allowing one tenant to act in another's scope. The exposure follows from how reviewer-agent receives drafted proposals awaiting review from edge-gateway and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Once the boundary is crossed the attacker can reach administrative functions and persist there. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Derive the tenant for reviewer-agent from the verified credential, ignore client-supplied tenant headers and test cross-tenant requests in CI. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "reviewer-agent",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Agent Runtime Zone/reviewer-agent",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "76e35aab882329d3",
            "findingId/v1": "E-17",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L3 \u2014 Agent Framework",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L3"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "A confused-deputy path lets a low-privilege caller ask tool-server-1 to act on tool call arguments and results using the privileges of worker-2. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on tool call arguments and results inherits the exposure. The caller gains rights that were never granted, which allows reading and changing data across tenants and approvals. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Pass the caller's authority through to tool-server-1 and evaluate the original caller's rights, never those of worker-2, for every delegated action. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "tool-server-1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Agent Runtime Zone/tool-server-1",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "5d94015036966adb",
