        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "Multi-tenant separation in tool-server-1 depends on a request header that clients can set, allowing one tenant to act in another's scope. tool-server-1 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges tool call arguments and results with worker-2 over HTTPS (TLS 1.3), so anything able to reach worker-2 can also reach this weakness. The caller gains rights that were never granted, which allows reading and changing data across tenants and approvals. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Derive the tenant for tool-server-1 from the verified credential, ignore client-supplied tenant headers and test cross-tenant requests in CI. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against tool-server-1, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
