        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "A privileged maintenance task of tool-server-1 can be triggered through a queue message that any producer on the bus may publish. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on tool call arguments and results inherits the exposure. The caller gains rights that were never granted, which allows reading and changing data across tenants and approvals. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Restrict who can publish maintenance messages that tool-server-1 acts on, sign them and require an authorised approver for destructive operations. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
