        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "embed-service-2 runs with broader permissions than its function needs, so a flaw in handling document chunks and query embeddings yields access to unrelated resources. The weakness sits at layer Foundation Model of the stack, so every workflow that depends on document chunks and query embeddings inherits the exposure. Once the boundary is crossed the attacker can reach administrative functions and persist there. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Reduce the permissions of embed-service-2 to the minimum for document chunks and query embeddings, drop capabilities it does not use and review the grants on a schedule. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for embed-service-2 and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
