        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "Object identifiers in requests to summarizer-llm are trusted without an ownership check, so a caller can read or change shipment records fed into summaries that belong to others. The weakness sits at layer Foundation Model of the stack, so every workflow that depends on shipment records fed into summaries inherits the exposure. Once the boundary is crossed the attacker can reach administrative functions and persist there. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Check ownership or entitlement for every object reference at summarizer-llm on the server, and deny by default when the check cannot be made. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for summarizer-llm and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
