          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent can start further agents or processes on request, so a compromised prompt can multiply its reach beyond the intended scope. trace-collector trusts intake-agent to pass free-text shipment requests along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Remove the ability of intake-agent to start other agents unless an operator pre-registers them, and enforce a global ceiling on active agents. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for intake-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
