            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "planner-agent retries failed actions on its own, repeating side effects such as bookings or messages when the first attempt partly succeeded. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on task plans and tool selections inherits the exposure. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Make the actions of planner-agent idempotent with request keys, cap retries and require confirmation before repeating any action with external effects. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to planner-agent."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
