        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "planner-agent does not limit the rate or total number of tool calls per task, so abuse of a costly tool goes unnoticed until the invoice arrives. planner-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges task plans and tool selections with trace-collector over OTLP over TLS, so anything able to reach trace-collector can also reach this weakness. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Apply per-task and per-tool quotas to planner-agent, alert on unusual call patterns and block calls once a cost ceiling is reached. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to planner-agent."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
