        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tool calls made by planner-agent are not tied to the end user, so the tool server cannot tell whose authority a request carries. Because planner-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of task plans and tool selections at once. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Propagate a signed end-user context with each tool call from planner-agent and make the tool server authorise against it, not against the agent identity. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
