        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "planner-agent invokes tools with arguments assembled from model output, so an attacker who shapes the output can call a tool with parameters the designer never allowed. memory-store trusts planner-agent to pass task plans and tool selections along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Validate every argument against the tool schema in planner-agent before the call, enforce allowlists of values and reject free-form commands. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to planner-agent."
          },
