        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "worker-2 can act on work orders and route candidates without a human approval step, so a manipulated plan executes high-impact actions with no checkpoint. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on work orders and route candidates inherits the exposure. Actions taken by the agent look legitimate in the logs, which slows detection and complicates rollback. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Require explicit human approval in worker-2 for actions above a defined impact threshold, and bind each approval to the exact action it covers. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against worker-2, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
