        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "tool-server-1 runs without a budget on steps or spend, so a loop or an adversarial task keeps it acting long after it stopped being useful. The exposure follows from how tool-server-1 receives tool call arguments and results from audit-ledger and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Set hard limits on steps, tool calls, runtime and spend for tool-server-1, stop on breach and report the stop reason to the operator. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against tool-server-1, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
