        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Delegation from worker-3 to tool-server-1 carries the full authority of the original session, so a low-trust sub-task can use high-trust rights. The exposure follows from how tool-server-1 receives tool call arguments and results from worker-3 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Actions taken by the agent look legitimate in the logs, which slows detection and complicates rollback. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Issue narrowly scoped, short-lived delegation grants to tool-server-1 and verify scope on every action instead of inheriting the parent session. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
