        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "queue-a2 does not limit the rate or total number of tool calls per task, so abuse of a costly tool goes unnoticed until the invoice arrives. queue-a2 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges task and result messages with planner-agent over NATS over TLS, so anything able to reach planner-agent can also reach this weakness. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Apply per-task and per-tool quotas to queue-a2, alert on unusual call patterns and block calls once a cost ceiling is reached. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "note",
