        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent can act on free-text shipment requests without a human approval step, so a manipulated plan executes high-impact actions with no checkpoint. embed-service-2 trusts intake-agent to pass free-text shipment requests along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. Actions taken by the agent look legitimate in the logs, which slows detection and complicates rollback. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Require explicit human approval in intake-agent for actions above a defined impact threshold, and bind each approval to the exact action it covers. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
