        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Memory written by tool-server-1 is trusted on later runs, so one poisoned entry changes the behaviour of every future task. The exposure follows from how tool-server-1 receives tool call arguments and results from worker-2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Tag memory entries with provenance and trust level, sanitise them on read and let operators review and expire entries written by tool-server-1. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to tool-server-1."
