        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Tool calls made by queue-a2 are not tied to the end user, so the tool server cannot tell whose authority a request carries. The weakness sits at layer Deployment Infrastructure of the stack, so every workflow that depends on task and result messages inherits the exposure. Actions taken by the agent look legitimate in the logs, which slows detection and complicates rollback. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Propagate a signed end-user context with each tool call from queue-a2 and make the tool server authorise against it, not against the agent identity. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for queue-a2 and record any exception with an expiry date."
