        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Interacting planning and routing agents amplify each other's outputs through feedback until their combined behaviour diverges from what any single agent was tested for, and per-agent safety checks never see the divergence. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on task plans and tool selections inherits the exposure. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Add fail-safe stop conditions for the planning loop, bound the actions each cycle may take and evaluate collective behaviour in staging. Recommended controls: bounded action scopes and behavioural baselining of the whole system."
          },
          "level": "warning",
