        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Worker agents coordinate through the shared message bus and memory so that each stays under its individual limits while together they exceed the authority intended for any one of them, and no single-agent control observes the combined behaviour. The exposure follows from how worker-2 receives work orders and route candidates from tool-server-1 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Monitor combined activity across agents, set aggregate budgets for groups of workers and separate the channels that agents can use to coordinate. Recommended controls: behavioural baselining of the collective agent system and alerts on coordinated bursts."
