        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "State persisted across runs lets a sleeper instruction written today change the behaviour of a scheduled run weeks later, after the original entry has left review and the context that explained it is gone. Because scheduler-1 serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of recurring planning triggers at once. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Expire persisted instructions, re-review any state that scheduled runs read and compare behaviour against pre-run snapshots. Recommended controls: provenance attestation for stored state and audit trails for every memory write."
