        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "An attacker splits a payload across several messages so that no single message trips the filter in front of edge-gateway. Because edge-gateway serves the Edge DMZ, a single failure here reaches each consumer of inbound API requests at once. The failure is probabilistic, so it may pass pre-release testing and appear only under adversarial input. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Evaluate the accumulated conversation in edge-gateway as a whole, track cumulative risk and reset trust when it crosses a threshold. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
