        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Prompt content logged by edge-gateway is later replayed to intake-agent for evaluation, carrying planted instructions into a trusted context. intake-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges free-text shipment requests with edge-gateway over HTTP/2 over mTLS, so anything able to reach edge-gateway can also reach this weakness. The failure is probabilistic, so it may pass pre-release testing and appear only under adversarial input. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Mark replayed prompts as untrusted when intake-agent processes them, and exclude logged content from any privileged instruction slot. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
