        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Indirect injection through documents retrieved for router-agent lets the author of a retrieved page steer the answer without ever talking to the system. Because router-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of subtask assignments at once. The answers or side effects of the model then serve the attacker's goal, and the behaviour can be repeated against every user of the component. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Score retrieved passages for instruction-like content before router-agent uses them, attribute every passage to its source and cap how much any one source contributes. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to router-agent."
