            "text": "router-agent passes conversation history from earlier turns into the model unchanged, so an injection planted earlier keeps working in later turns. The exposure follows from how router-agent receives subtask assignments from planner-agent and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The answers or side effects of the model then serve the attacker's goal, and the behaviour can be repeated against every user of the component. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Re-screen conversation history on each turn in router-agent, expire old turns and mark which turns came from untrusted sources. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against router-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
