        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "A user message crafted to look like a system directive persuades trace-collector to disclose its configuration or ignore its rules. The weakness sits at layer Evaluation and Observability of the stack, so every workflow that depends on prompts, completions and tool traces inherits the exposure. The answers or side effects of the model then serve the attacker's goal, and the behaviour can be repeated against every user of the component. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Keep the system guidance for trace-collector out of reach of user text, test against known jailbreak patterns in CI and refuse requests that reference hidden instructions. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for trace-collector and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "error",
