          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Evaluation labels consumed from eval-runner are produced by a judge model that can itself be influenced by planted traces. The weakness sits at layer Evaluation and Observability of the stack, so every workflow that depends on replayed traces and judge verdicts inherits the exposure. The failure is probabilistic, so it may pass pre-release testing and appear only under adversarial input. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Calibrate the judge on a human-labelled subset from eval-runner, rotate judge prompts and flag results that drift from the human baseline. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for eval-runner and record any exception with an expiry date."
