        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "policy-engine follows links and files named in guardrail rules and approval decisions, which turns a harmless-looking request into a fetch of attacker-controlled content. The weakness sits at layer Security and Compliance of the stack, so every workflow that depends on guardrail rules and approval decisions inherits the exposure. The failure is probabilistic, so it may pass pre-release testing and appear only under adversarial input. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Restrict what policy-engine may fetch to an allowlist of domains and types, fetch through a sandbox and present the results as untrusted data. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to policy-engine."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
