        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Instructions hidden in guardrail rules and approval decisions reach the prompt of policy-engine and override its system guidance, because content and instructions share one context. The weakness sits at layer Security and Compliance of the stack, so every workflow that depends on guardrail rules and approval decisions inherits the exposure. The answers or side effects of the model then serve the attacker's goal, and the behaviour can be repeated against every user of the component. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Separate instructions from content in the prompts of policy-engine, delimit untrusted text and run an injection classifier before the model sees it. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to policy-engine."
