          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "model-gateway passes conversation history from earlier turns into the model unchanged, so an injection planted earlier keeps working in later turns. planner-agent trusts model-gateway to pass prompts and completions along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The failure is probabilistic, so it may pass pre-release testing and appear only under adversarial input. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Re-screen conversation history on each turn in model-gateway, expire old turns and mark which turns came from untrusted sources. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to model-gateway."
