        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent emits URLs that downstream services fetch, so an attacker can make internal addresses part of the output and trigger server-side requests. trace-collector trusts intake-agent to pass free-text shipment requests along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The unsafe output reaches an interpreter that trusts it, turning a text generation problem into code or request execution. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Validate URLs from intake-agent against an allowlist, resolve and block private ranges before fetching, and fetch from a restricted network. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for intake-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "note",
