        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Structured output from intake-agent is trusted by queue-a2 as already validated, so a malformed field flows straight into business logic. Because intake-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of free-text shipment requests at once. Downstream components cannot tell the model's output from validated input, so no later layer is likely to catch it. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Validate the output of intake-agent against a strict schema in queue-a2, treat it as untrusted input and reject anything that fails. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to intake-agent."
