        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "File paths or names produced by intake-agent are used to write files, letting crafted output reach locations outside the intended directory. intake-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges free-text shipment requests with edge-gateway over HTTP/2 over mTLS, so anything able to reach edge-gateway can also reach this weakness. Downstream components cannot tell the model's output from validated input, so no later layer is likely to catch it. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Generate file names for intake-agent on the server, confine writes to a sandbox directory and reject any path component supplied by the model. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "intake-agent",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Agent Runtime Zone/intake-agent",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "4bcca12a86cc1a88",
            "findingId/v1": "OI-4",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L3 \u2014 Agent Framework",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L3"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Model output from intake-agent is inserted into a rendered page without encoding, so crafted output executes script in an operator's browser. intake-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges free-text shipment requests with trace-collector over OTLP over TLS, so anything able to reach trace-collector can also reach this weakness. The unsafe output reaches an interpreter that trusts it, turning a text generation problem into code or request execution. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Encode model output from intake-agent for its destination, render it as text by default and apply a content security policy that blocks inline script. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for intake-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
