        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent emits URLs that downstream services fetch, so an attacker can make internal addresses part of the output and trigger server-side requests. The exposure follows from how intake-agent receives free-text shipment requests from embed-service-2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Downstream components cannot tell the model's output from validated input, so no later layer is likely to catch it. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Validate URLs from intake-agent against an allowlist, resolve and block private ranges before fetching, and fetch from a restricted network. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for intake-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
