          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "planner-agent emits URLs that downstream services fetch, so an attacker can make internal addresses part of the output and trigger server-side requests. planner-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges task plans and tool selections with model-gateway over HTTPS (TLS 1.3), so anything able to reach model-gateway can also reach this weakness. The unsafe output reaches an interpreter that trusts it, turning a text generation problem into code or request execution. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Validate URLs from planner-agent against an allowlist, resolve and block private ranges before fetching, and fetch from a restricted network. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
