        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Markdown or HTML produced by planner-agent contains remote images that leak data when a client renders it. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on task plans and tool selections inherits the exposure. Downstream components cannot tell the model's output from validated input, so no later layer is likely to catch it. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Strip remote resources from the output of planner-agent before display, proxy images through a controlled service and disable automatic loading. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to planner-agent."
