          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Text generated by summarizer-llm is placed into a database query or shell argument without parameterisation, allowing the model to be steered into injection. summarizer-llm runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges shipment records fed into summaries with worker-3 over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach worker-3 can also reach this weakness. The unsafe output reaches an interpreter that trusts it, turning a text generation problem into code or request execution. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Never build queries or commands from model output of summarizer-llm: use parameterised calls and fixed argument vectors with allowlisted values. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for summarizer-llm and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
