          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "summarizer-llm emits URLs that downstream services fetch, so an attacker can make internal addresses part of the output and trigger server-side requests. feature-store-2 trusts summarizer-llm to pass shipment records fed into summaries along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The unsafe output reaches an interpreter that trusts it, turning a text generation problem into code or request execution. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Validate URLs from summarizer-llm against an allowlist, resolve and block private ranges before fetching, and fetch from a restricted network. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to trace-collector so that responders see them in one place."
          },
