        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent fabricates reference numbers and clause citations that look real, which operators then paste into official documents. The exposure follows from how intake-agent receives free-text shipment requests from embed-service-2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The mistake looks authoritative, so it is rarely questioned until a downstream party objects. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Verify identifiers and citations produced by intake-agent against authoritative systems before display, and mark unverifiable ones clearly. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against intake-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "warning",
