          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent states carrier rules and customs requirements as fact without grounding them in a cited source, so an operator may act on an invented rule. intake-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges free-text shipment requests with trace-collector over OTLP over TLS, so anything able to reach trace-collector can also reach this weakness. The mistake looks authoritative, so it is rarely questioned until a downstream party objects. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Require intake-agent to cite a retrievable source for each factual claim, show the citations and decline to answer when none is found. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against intake-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
