            "text": "Confident wording from reviewer-agent hides low retrieval quality, so operators cannot tell a grounded answer from a guess. Because reviewer-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of drafted proposals awaiting review at once. The mistake looks authoritative, so it is rarely questioned until a downstream party objects. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Expose retrieval strength alongside the answers of reviewer-agent and switch to an explicit uncertainty message below a threshold. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against reviewer-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
