        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent adopts a persona that presents itself as a named colleague, so operators trust its suggestions more than its accuracy warrants. embed-service-2 trusts intake-agent to pass free-text shipment requests along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The effect builds over time as users come to rely on the agent's tone instead of its evidence. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Disclose that intake-agent is an automated agent at the start of each session and avoid human-like names or personal claims. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for intake-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
