        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Persuasive phrasing from intake-agent pushes operators to approve proposals quickly, which reduces careful review. The exposure follows from how intake-agent receives free-text shipment requests from queue-a2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. People defer to the agent more than its reliability justifies, which weakens the human oversight the design depends on. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Neutralise urgency and pressure wording in intake-agent, present alternatives with their trade-offs and require a deliberate action to approve. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against intake-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
