        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent claims certainty it does not have when summarising shipment risk, and customers rely on the stated confidence. The exposure follows from how intake-agent receives free-text shipment requests from trace-collector and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. People defer to the agent more than its reliability justifies, which weakens the human oversight the design depends on. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Attach calibrated confidence and the basis for each claim to the output of intake-agent, and block unqualified guarantees in customer-facing text. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through trace-collector when the control fires."
          },
