          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent adopts a persona that presents itself as a named colleague, so operators trust its suggestions more than its accuracy warrants. Because intake-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of free-text shipment requests at once. People defer to the agent more than its reliability justifies, which weakens the human oversight the design depends on. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Disclose that intake-agent is an automated agent at the start of each session and avoid human-like names or personal claims. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against intake-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
